WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.048 --> 00:00:07.924
[Reacher] <i>Grew up in the
military. worked in the military.</i>

2
00:00:07.925 --> 00:00:09.801
<i>Always told where to
go. when to be there.</i>

3
00:00:09.802 --> 00:00:11.428
<i>Now I see my country
on my own terms.</i>

4
00:00:11.429 --> 00:00:14.556
<i>Motels. cash. fake
names. Travel light.</i>

5
00:00:14.557 --> 00:00:17.142
<i>Mostly I take buses or
hitchhike. You get used to it.</i>

6
00:00:17.143 --> 00:00:18.560
[Finlay] <i>Commanded the 110th</i>

7
00:00:18.561 --> 00:00:21.521
<i>Special Investigations Unit
of the Military Police.</i>

8
00:00:21.522 --> 00:00:23.148
You refer to these
special investigators

9
00:00:23.149 --> 00:00:24.607
<i>as your team?</i>

10
00:00:24.608 --> 00:00:26.985
<i>They're soldiers.
You need new friends.</i>

11
00:00:26.986 --> 00:00:28.779
<i>But you know we're
more than that. right?</i>

12
00:00:30.406 --> 00:00:31.406
[grunts]

13
00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:35.910
[shouting]

14
00:00:37.747 --> 00:00:40.707
[pained cries]

15
00:00:40.708 --> 00:00:43.001
[Reacher] <i>Hundred thousand
years ago there were people</i>

16
00:00:43.002 --> 00:00:45.670
<i>who stayed by the campfire.
and people who wandered.</i>

17
00:00:45.671 --> 00:00:47.213
[dramatic music playing]

18
00:00:47.214 --> 00:00:50.633
<i>I'm pretty sure I'm a direct
descendant of the wandering type.</i>

19
00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:52.594
<i>It's just who I am.</i>

20
00:00:52.595 --> 00:00:54.096
<i>♪ ♪</i>

21
00:00:59.351 --> 00:01:01.102
[♪ The Smithereens:
"Blood and Roses"]

22
00:01:01.103 --> 00:01:02.938
♪ ♪

23
00:01:15.159 --> 00:01:19.120
<i>♪ It was long ago ♪</i>

24
00:01:19.121 --> 00:01:23.166
<i>♪ Seems like yesterday ♪</i>

25
00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:27.170
<i>♪ Saw you standing in the rain ♪</i>

26
00:01:27.171 --> 00:01:31.382
<i>♪ Then I heard you say ♪</i>

27
00:01:31.383 --> 00:01:35.053
<i>♪ I want to love. but
it comes out wrong ♪</i>

28
00:01:35.054 --> 00:01:38.223
<i>♪ I want to live but
I don't belong...</i>

29
00:01:38.224 --> 00:01:40.350
I don't care about
process. just product.

30
00:01:40.351 --> 00:01:43.186
And this product
emotes feelings.

31
00:01:43.187 --> 00:01:46.689
Hey. man. greatest song
on the subject of water.

32
00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:48.566
Ocean. river. stream.
it doesn't matter.

33
00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:51.778
It's gotta be "Surfin'
Safari." right? So?

34
00:01:51.779 --> 00:01:54.739
"Surfin' Safari's" a rip-off of
Chuck Berry's "Sweet Little Sixteen."

35
00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:56.282
so that knocks it
out on principle.

36
00:01:56.283 --> 00:01:58.785
[scoffs] Oh. man.

37
00:01:58.786 --> 00:02:01.204
Solid answer. What
can I do for you?

38
00:02:01.205 --> 00:02:02.622
Your sign says you buy vinyl.

39
00:02:02.623 --> 00:02:05.250
<i>♪ Her blood ran cold
and then she said...</i>

40
00:02:05.251 --> 00:02:08.378
<i>Ethel Merman Disco Album.</i>

41
00:02:08.379 --> 00:02:11.172
- Are you shitting me?
- But this is a college town.

42
00:02:11.173 --> 00:02:13.675
Some hipster will
buy 'em to be ironic.

43
00:02:13.676 --> 00:02:14.926
No...

44
00:02:14.927 --> 00:02:17.470
- <i>♪ I close my eyes and I see ♪</i>
- [truck engine revving]

45
00:02:17.471 --> 00:02:19.598
<i>♪ Blood and roses ♪</i>

46
00:02:40.953 --> 00:02:42.955
[tires squealing]

47
00:02:44.707 --> 00:02:46.000
What the hell?

48
00:02:47.585 --> 00:02:50.421
[tires squealing]

49
00:02:51.964 --> 00:02:53.673
[groans]

50
00:02:53.674 --> 00:02:56.259
[tense music playing]

51
00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:58.387
Oh. Oh. no! No. no. no. no. no!

52
00:02:59.471 --> 00:03:01.932
[whimpering] Okay.

53
00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:06.060
- Okay...
- [door bells jingle]

54
00:03:06.061 --> 00:03:07.562
- [explosion]
- [gasps]

55
00:03:07.563 --> 00:03:09.106
[car alarm blaring]

56
00:03:11.233 --> 00:03:12.902
[bystanders screaming]

57
00:03:13.611 --> 00:03:15.862
[engine revving]

58
00:03:15.863 --> 00:03:17.907
[tires squealing]

59
00:03:27.666 --> 00:03:29.626
- [gunshot]
- [gasps]

60
00:03:29.627 --> 00:03:31.169
[panting]

61
00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.172
- No. Please?
- I'm not gonna hurt you.

62
00:03:34.256 --> 00:03:37.175
[panting]

63
00:03:37.176 --> 00:03:38.593
[groans]

64
00:03:38.594 --> 00:03:40.929
- Get in.
- Well. I...

65
00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.056
They may have backup on the way.

66
00:03:43.057 --> 00:03:44.891
[man] Hey!

67
00:03:44.892 --> 00:03:46.977
[groans]

68
00:03:49.605 --> 00:03:52.440
[tense music playing]

69
00:03:52.441 --> 00:03:53.983
You shot a cop.

70
00:03:53.984 --> 00:03:55.610
I didn't know.

71
00:03:55.611 --> 00:03:57.862
- I thought he was pulling a gun.
- [siren wailing]

72
00:03:57.863 --> 00:03:59.865
- We got to go. Now!
- What?

73
00:04:02.618 --> 00:04:05.037
[tires squealing]

74
00:04:07.623 --> 00:04:10.250
[siren approaching]

75
00:04:11.669 --> 00:04:13.920
♪ ♪

76
00:04:13.921 --> 00:04:16.006
Why are people
trying to kidnap you?

77
00:04:17.091 --> 00:04:19.217
[siren wailing]

78
00:04:19.218 --> 00:04:21.052
[Reacher] Campus police?

79
00:04:21.053 --> 00:04:23.096
- Are you shitting me?
- Pull over.

80
00:04:23.097 --> 00:04:24.597
I killed a cop with
an illegal gun!

81
00:04:24.598 --> 00:04:25.765
Well. it was an accident.

82
00:04:25.766 --> 00:04:28.059
I'm not explaining
my way out of this.

83
00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:29.687
Get down!

84
00:04:35.401 --> 00:04:36.819
[panting] Look out!

85
00:04:37.361 --> 00:04:39.571
[tires squealing]

86
00:04:42.324 --> 00:04:44.743
[siren continues wailing]

87
00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.043
[panting]

88
00:04:54.044 --> 00:04:55.962
Hang on.

89
00:04:55.963 --> 00:04:57.047
- [tires squealing]
- Oh!

90
00:04:58.716 --> 00:05:00.467
[tires squealing]

91
00:05:03.721 --> 00:05:04.971
[panting]

92
00:05:04.972 --> 00:05:07.224
♪ ♪

93
00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:10.393
You could have killed 'em!

94
00:05:10.394 --> 00:05:12.270
I slowed 'em enough
to limit the impact.

95
00:05:12.271 --> 00:05:14.148
But I bet they
called the real cops.

96
00:05:15.232 --> 00:05:17.734
I got to find a new ride.

97
00:05:17.735 --> 00:05:19.820
[slow. suspenseful
music playing]

98
00:05:32.458 --> 00:05:34.293
Uh...

99
00:05:35.294 --> 00:05:37.462
We're only a few
miles from campus.

100
00:05:37.463 --> 00:05:40.090
There could be more kidnappers
coming up right behind us.

101
00:05:41.717 --> 00:05:43.509
You're gonna steal it?

102
00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:45.219
Parked out back
with a sun shade?

103
00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:46.929
[rummaging]

104
00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.848
Probably belongs to an employee
who won't notice it's missing

105
00:05:48.849 --> 00:05:50.349
till tonight.

106
00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.894
Gives me a head start.

107
00:05:52.895 --> 00:05:55.480
Keep an eye out.

108
00:05:55.481 --> 00:05:58.733
Aah. Hey. where'd you
learn to do all this stuff?

109
00:05:58.734 --> 00:06:01.194
Steal cars. drive like that?

110
00:06:01.195 --> 00:06:03.571
- Shoot people?
- Army.

111
00:06:03.572 --> 00:06:05.490
Other stuff I picked
up here and there.

112
00:06:05.491 --> 00:06:07.242
[grunts]

113
00:06:10.204 --> 00:06:11.454
You got a phone?

114
00:06:11.455 --> 00:06:12.997
Uh. why?

115
00:06:12.998 --> 00:06:15.374
So you can call for a ride.

116
00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:17.502
Tell 'em you're in shock and
can't remember what I look like.

117
00:06:17.503 --> 00:06:19.796
What? No! You can't
just leave me here.

118
00:06:19.797 --> 00:06:20.963
What if those guys find me?

119
00:06:20.964 --> 00:06:23.216
What am I supposed to
do? Take you to the cops?

120
00:06:23.217 --> 00:06:24.967
I can't do that
after what I did.

121
00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:26.260
So then take me home.

122
00:06:26.261 --> 00:06:27.929
- [crackling]
- No.

123
00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:30.264
[engine starts]

124
00:06:30.265 --> 00:06:32.475
Done enough for you for one day.

125
00:06:32.476 --> 00:06:34.977
I got to disappear.

126
00:06:34.978 --> 00:06:36.354
Please.

127
00:06:36.355 --> 00:06:39.816
I'm a drifter who used an
unlicensed gun to kill a cop.

128
00:06:39.817 --> 00:06:42.110
I'm not taking any chances.

129
00:06:42.111 --> 00:06:43.861
I'm getting lost.

130
00:06:43.862 --> 00:06:45.363
My dad's rich.

131
00:06:45.364 --> 00:06:47.532
And connected. He
can... he can help you.

132
00:06:47.533 --> 00:06:49.283
Why would he do that?

133
00:06:49.284 --> 00:06:51.370
Well. you saved his son.

134
00:06:52.538 --> 00:06:54.956
That cop was an accident. Right?

135
00:06:54.957 --> 00:06:57.291
So. look. he'll j...
he'll just be grateful

136
00:06:57.292 --> 00:06:59.836
that you kept me from
getting kidnapped again.

137
00:06:59.837 --> 00:07:02.172
- Again?
- First time was five years ago.

138
00:07:03.257 --> 00:07:04.549
That what happened to your ear?

139
00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:06.008
They wanted to make a point.

140
00:07:06.009 --> 00:07:08.719
- 'Cause your dad wouldn't pay the ransom?
- Yeah.

141
00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:11.014
After he got my ear
in the mail. he paid.

142
00:07:14.059 --> 00:07:15.977
Not as bad as you did.

143
00:07:15.978 --> 00:07:18.604
Kidnapping is a rare
crime in this country.

144
00:07:18.605 --> 00:07:20.731
Pretty unlucky it almost
happened to you twice.

145
00:07:20.732 --> 00:07:22.233
What does your father
do for a living?

146
00:07:22.234 --> 00:07:23.442
Imports rugs.

147
00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:25.736
That all he imports?

148
00:07:25.737 --> 00:07:27.905
He's just a rug merchant.

149
00:07:27.906 --> 00:07:29.907
But he's got generational wealth.
and that makes me a target.

150
00:07:29.908 --> 00:07:33.286
So the guy who got blown up in
your car wasn't your driver.

151
00:07:33.287 --> 00:07:35.581
- He was your bodyguard.
- Yeah.

152
00:07:36.665 --> 00:07:39.000
Tell your dad to hire
a better one next time.

153
00:07:39.001 --> 00:07:41.085
Guy who took a run
at you was a pro.

154
00:07:41.086 --> 00:07:42.712
If it hadn't been for
me. it would have worked.

155
00:07:42.713 --> 00:07:44.589
Okay. so then. take me home

156
00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:46.340
and let my dad repay
you for what you did.

157
00:07:46.341 --> 00:07:49.093
Y-You want to disappear? You-you
need money? He has money.

158
00:07:49.094 --> 00:07:50.429
Please.

159
00:07:56.268 --> 00:07:57.560
You got a name. kid?

160
00:07:57.561 --> 00:08:00.605
Richard. Richard Beck.

161
00:08:00.606 --> 00:08:03.357
[distant siren wailing]

162
00:08:03.358 --> 00:08:05.401
- Get in. Richard.
- [sighs]

163
00:08:05.402 --> 00:08:08.071
[suspenseful music playing]

164
00:08:12.492 --> 00:08:14.203
[seabirds chirping]

165
00:08:15.579 --> 00:08:17.581
♪ ♪

166
00:08:19.124 --> 00:08:20.834
[waves crashing]

167
00:08:30.219 --> 00:08:32.221
♪ ♪

168
00:08:46.526 --> 00:08:48.945
- Get out of the car.
- [Richard] Yeah. it's all right. Paulie.

169
00:08:48.946 --> 00:08:50.488
I talked to my dad and
told him we were coming.

170
00:08:50.489 --> 00:08:52.198
I don't give a shit.

171
00:08:52.199 --> 00:08:53.700
Get out.

172
00:08:54.785 --> 00:08:57.078
No.

173
00:08:57.079 --> 00:08:58.704
Just let him do it.

174
00:08:58.705 --> 00:09:02.042
- He's rude.
- Please.

175
00:09:12.761 --> 00:09:14.304
♪ ♪

176
00:09:25.399 --> 00:09:26.857
[Paulie] You know what
I'm hoping to find?

177
00:09:26.858 --> 00:09:29.736
More HGH and a
hypodermic needle?

178
00:09:32.447 --> 00:09:33.906
A reason to kick
your ass. shithead.

179
00:09:33.907 --> 00:09:37.202
And maybe you just
gave it to me.

180
00:09:38.287 --> 00:09:40.496
Uh...

181
00:09:40.497 --> 00:09:44.125
His-his gun is in the
glove compartment. Paulie.

182
00:09:44.126 --> 00:09:46.295
Here. just take it.

183
00:09:48.797 --> 00:09:50.131
Why is it empty?

184
00:09:50.132 --> 00:09:52.091
Because I shot all the bullets.

185
00:09:52.092 --> 00:09:53.677
[revolver clicks]

186
00:09:56.763 --> 00:09:59.808
[buzzer sounds]

187
00:10:05.272 --> 00:10:07.481
Lot of security
for a rug merchant.

188
00:10:07.482 --> 00:10:09.900
I told you. He's rich.

189
00:10:09.901 --> 00:10:13.405
[suspenseful music playing]

190
00:10:19.494 --> 00:10:20.870
[Reacher] <i>Your dad's
employees always</i>

191
00:10:20.871 --> 00:10:22.998
talk like that to
his son's friends?

192
00:10:24.374 --> 00:10:28.211
Paul Van Hoven does
whatever he wants.

193
00:10:37.095 --> 00:10:39.389
Yeah. Oh. are... are you hungry?

194
00:10:40.474 --> 00:10:41.599
Sure.

195
00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:43.101
I'll make him a plate.

196
00:10:44.186 --> 00:10:45.644
I can just take that
one on the counter.

197
00:10:45.645 --> 00:10:49.190
That's not for you. And
you don't have time to eat.

198
00:10:49.191 --> 00:10:50.441
Beck wants to see you.

199
00:10:50.442 --> 00:10:53.069
Office is upstairs. down
the hall and to the right.

200
00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:54.570
Uh. I can show you.

201
00:10:54.571 --> 00:10:56.907
No. He wants to see him alone.

202
00:10:59.368 --> 00:11:02.537
And that's Chapman
Duke. head of security.

203
00:11:03.747 --> 00:11:06.207
Why is he eating outside?

204
00:11:06.208 --> 00:11:09.419
Who knows? But you
better do what he says.

205
00:11:24.101 --> 00:11:25.643
Mr. Reacher.

206
00:11:25.644 --> 00:11:27.353
Just... Reacher.

207
00:11:27.354 --> 00:11:28.855
Noted.

208
00:11:30.816 --> 00:11:32.775
I'm Zachary Beck.

209
00:11:32.776 --> 00:11:35.528
You had some morning.

210
00:11:35.529 --> 00:11:38.072
I bet you could use a drink.

211
00:11:38.073 --> 00:11:40.741
This is 50-year-old Macallan.

212
00:11:40.742 --> 00:11:43.369
I only open it for my top
business associates...

213
00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:45.664
and people who
save my son's life.

214
00:11:55.924 --> 00:11:57.509
Suit yourself.

215
00:11:59.136 --> 00:12:00.429
Have a seat there.

216
00:12:07.769 --> 00:12:09.145
Okay. fine.

217
00:12:09.146 --> 00:12:10.981
Don't sit.

218
00:12:12.065 --> 00:12:13.983
I'm sure you heard what Richard told
me about the attempted kidnapping

219
00:12:13.984 --> 00:12:15.734
when he called me from the car.

220
00:12:15.735 --> 00:12:17.236
What can you add to that?

221
00:12:17.237 --> 00:12:19.530
Just that the guy you hired
to look after him was useless.

222
00:12:19.531 --> 00:12:21.824
- You're speaking ill of the dead.
- A ratty old pickup

223
00:12:21.825 --> 00:12:24.118
hanging around a
rich-kid college town?

224
00:12:24.119 --> 00:12:26.454
What kind of bodyguard
doesn't clock that?

225
00:12:26.455 --> 00:12:28.539
But you noticed a
detail that small.

226
00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:29.708
I tend to do that.

227
00:12:31.293 --> 00:12:32.918
What makes you so good
at threat assessment?

228
00:12:32.919 --> 00:12:35.629
I was in the Army. MP.

229
00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:37.756
I was trying to unload records

230
00:12:37.757 --> 00:12:39.341
- for some extra cash.
- Is that your job?

231
00:12:39.342 --> 00:12:43.096
Selling used records in
New England college towns?

232
00:12:46.099 --> 00:12:47.266
There a lot of money in that?

233
00:12:47.267 --> 00:12:49.351
- Don't have a job.
- So. how do you pay the rent?

234
00:12:49.352 --> 00:12:51.270
Don't have a home.

235
00:12:51.271 --> 00:12:54.064
- I move around a lot.
- With a gun?

236
00:12:54.065 --> 00:12:56.692
Wherever I go. trouble
just seems to find me.

237
00:12:56.693 --> 00:12:59.987
I understand you accidentally
killed a police officer.

238
00:12:59.988 --> 00:13:01.780
I just need a place to
lie low for a few days

239
00:13:01.781 --> 00:13:04.241
and then some money to buy a
fake I.D. for a clean start.

240
00:13:04.242 --> 00:13:05.702
That's no small ask.

241
00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:09.539
But I do owe you.

242
00:13:11.583 --> 00:13:14.084
Let me think it over and I'll...

243
00:13:14.085 --> 00:13:15.920
figure out the best
way I can be of help.

244
00:13:15.921 --> 00:13:17.338
Okay.

245
00:13:17.339 --> 00:13:18.715
Duke.

246
00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:23.469
Sir. could you show Mr. Reacher
back to the kitchen. please?

247
00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:26.223
I believe Agnes has some
nice shepherd's pie.

248
00:13:38.068 --> 00:13:41.112
I gripped it firmly so you'll
have a clear set of prints to run.

249
00:13:44.699 --> 00:13:46.242
[Beck] Don't be
offended. Mr. Reacher.

250
00:13:46.243 --> 00:13:47.786
Just need to know who you are.

251
00:13:50.789 --> 00:13:53.291
I'm the guy who saved
your son's other ear.

252
00:13:56.795 --> 00:13:59.172
♪ ♪

253
00:14:05.845 --> 00:14:08.222
If I go in to hit the head.
you gonna hold it for me?

254
00:14:08.223 --> 00:14:09.765
If I want to.

255
00:14:09.766 --> 00:14:11.851
[soft clattering]

256
00:14:14.938 --> 00:14:17.189
Hey. hey. where are you going?

257
00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:19.608
- To check on the kid.
- We'll take care of him.

258
00:14:19.609 --> 00:14:21.653
Like your guy did this morning?

259
00:14:45.051 --> 00:14:46.802
You forgot to add
the guard house.

260
00:14:46.803 --> 00:14:49.139
[Richard] No. I didn't.

261
00:14:50.724 --> 00:14:52.559
How was your talk with my dad?

262
00:14:53.852 --> 00:14:56.270
He has trust issues.

263
00:14:56.271 --> 00:14:59.190
Surprised he hasn't come to check on
you. Considering all that happened.

264
00:15:00.483 --> 00:15:02.569
We talked on the phone.
He knows I'm okay.

265
00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:08.158
He'll check on me soon.

266
00:15:10.493 --> 00:15:11.870
Okay.

267
00:15:16.291 --> 00:15:18.293
Where's your mother?

268
00:15:19.836 --> 00:15:23.757
[Richard] Since I was four.
St. Sebastian's Cemetery.

269
00:15:34.184 --> 00:15:36.811
You only paint what you
see out those windows?

270
00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:40.606
[Richard] Paint what you know.

271
00:15:40.607 --> 00:15:42.067
You ever paint. Reacher?

272
00:15:43.401 --> 00:15:45.486
No.

273
00:15:45.487 --> 00:15:48.573
Well. if you did.
what would it be of?

274
00:15:50.283 --> 00:15:52.368
I don't know.

275
00:15:52.369 --> 00:15:54.079
Dogs. maybe.

276
00:15:55.538 --> 00:15:57.374
[Duke] Beck wants to see you.

277
00:16:00.126 --> 00:16:02.544
Guess it's back to the office.

278
00:16:02.545 --> 00:16:04.254
We're not going
back to the office.

279
00:16:04.255 --> 00:16:06.341
[ominous music playing]

280
00:16:17.477 --> 00:16:18.687
Sit.

281
00:16:20.522 --> 00:16:23.482
Today's excitement
made the news.

282
00:16:23.483 --> 00:16:25.610
Lot of buzz for a college town.

283
00:16:27.237 --> 00:16:28.445
I get made?

284
00:16:28.446 --> 00:16:30.989
[Beck] Guys at the record shop
gave a general description.

285
00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:35.120
but that could match any
inside linebacker. so...

286
00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:38.039
...no one knows who you are.

287
00:16:39.874 --> 00:16:41.292
But we do.

288
00:16:42.961 --> 00:16:44.169
We ran your prints.

289
00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:46.672
That was fast.

290
00:16:46.673 --> 00:16:48.257
Must have some
serious connections.

291
00:16:48.258 --> 00:16:50.677
Everything we do
here is serious.

292
00:16:54.264 --> 00:16:56.098
Your record is impressive.

293
00:16:56.099 --> 00:16:57.725
West Point graduate.

294
00:16:57.726 --> 00:16:59.143
Two Silver Stars.

295
00:16:59.144 --> 00:17:00.644
Purple Heart.

296
00:17:00.645 --> 00:17:02.062
[Paulie] Green
clovers. blue diamonds.

297
00:17:02.063 --> 00:17:04.898
He's a fucking bowl
of Lucky Charms.

298
00:17:04.899 --> 00:17:06.400
Paulie was in the Army. too.

299
00:17:06.401 --> 00:17:08.486
He doesn't like officers.

300
00:17:10.155 --> 00:17:12.865
You failed the OCS exam.

301
00:17:12.866 --> 00:17:14.366
Not surprised.

302
00:17:14.367 --> 00:17:16.327
You don't look like
you could spell OCS.

303
00:17:17.412 --> 00:17:19.663
[Beck] What if I could do more than
give you a couple bucks. Reacher?

304
00:17:19.664 --> 00:17:23.167
At a time we're short a man.
it appears we're under attack.

305
00:17:23.168 --> 00:17:24.752
'Cause you're a rug merchant?

306
00:17:24.753 --> 00:17:27.755
Because I'm wealthy.
And powerful.

307
00:17:27.756 --> 00:17:29.840
So I hear.

308
00:17:29.841 --> 00:17:31.717
And because of that.
you want to hire me?

309
00:17:31.718 --> 00:17:33.011
Maybe.

310
00:17:35.138 --> 00:17:38.057
But first a little test.

311
00:17:43.521 --> 00:17:45.022
What am I supposed
to do with that?

312
00:17:45.023 --> 00:17:47.108
You're gonna play Russian
roulette. asshole.

313
00:17:48.693 --> 00:17:52.029
Federal law prevents you from asking me
if I'm married during a job interview.

314
00:17:52.030 --> 00:17:53.530
so I'm pretty sure
this isn't allowed.

315
00:17:53.531 --> 00:17:56.909
I need to see if
you have any stones.

316
00:17:56.910 --> 00:17:58.411
If you can follow orders.

317
00:17:59.496 --> 00:18:02.414
- To work for a rug merchant.
- You shot a cop.

318
00:18:02.415 --> 00:18:04.416
We can turn you in or you
can do what you're told.

319
00:18:04.417 --> 00:18:06.044
Those are your choices.

320
00:18:10.799 --> 00:18:12.801
♪ ♪

321
00:18:24.103 --> 00:18:26.606
What if I just
shoot you instead?

322
00:18:28.107 --> 00:18:29.733
That would be the
last thing you do.

323
00:18:29.734 --> 00:18:31.069
[gun clicks]

324
00:18:47.335 --> 00:18:49.796
Good. We got that
out of the way.

325
00:18:53.466 --> 00:18:54.968
[revolver cylinder
spinning. clicks]

326
00:18:57.720 --> 00:19:00.598
[revolver cylinder
spinning. clicks]

327
00:19:02.517 --> 00:19:04.310
You proved your point.

328
00:19:10.275 --> 00:19:13.278
Welcome to the team. Reacher.
Duke will get you squared away.

329
00:19:22.871 --> 00:19:24.454
You're kidding.

330
00:19:24.455 --> 00:19:26.081
Thought I was on the team.

331
00:19:26.082 --> 00:19:27.875
I got enough crazy on
my hands with Paulie.

332
00:19:27.876 --> 00:19:30.252
I don't need your big ass walking
around here with a gun. too.

333
00:19:30.253 --> 00:19:31.503
I'm not crazy.

334
00:19:31.504 --> 00:19:34.549
I know the bullet didn't have
any powder in it. It's a dud.

335
00:19:43.766 --> 00:19:45.767
What would you have done
if I had killed myself?

336
00:19:45.768 --> 00:19:47.937
Same thing we did
with the last guy.

337
00:20:03.286 --> 00:20:04.662
Let's go!

338
00:20:14.589 --> 00:20:16.591
♪ ♪

339
00:20:19.802 --> 00:20:21.804
[lock clicking]

340
00:20:23.014 --> 00:20:25.641
You start first thing in the
morning. You're locked in until then.

341
00:20:25.642 --> 00:20:26.808
Why?

342
00:20:26.809 --> 00:20:28.602
Because Beck might trust
you now. but I don't.

343
00:20:28.603 --> 00:20:31.064
- What if I don't like that arrangement?
- Call the cops.

344
00:20:32.982 --> 00:20:34.858
[lock clicks]

345
00:20:34.859 --> 00:20:36.861
[footsteps receding]

346
00:20:40.323 --> 00:20:42.325
[mysterious music playing]

347
00:21:04.347 --> 00:21:05.556
[beeps]

348
00:21:07.433 --> 00:21:09.518
- [Duffy] <i>Yeah?</i>
- I'm in.

349
00:21:09.519 --> 00:21:11.604
[thunder crashing]

350
00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:44.845
[mother] Wait.

351
00:21:44.846 --> 00:21:46.304
Wait! Wait!

352
00:21:46.305 --> 00:21:47.515
Wait!

353
00:21:53.730 --> 00:21:57.191
Hey. We'll catch
the next one. okay?

354
00:22:11.956 --> 00:22:13.498
Don't do it.

355
00:22:13.499 --> 00:22:14.792
What?

356
00:22:16.294 --> 00:22:19.130
You're gonna take the next bus with
that woman and steal from her bag.

357
00:22:20.757 --> 00:22:22.091
Fuck you.

358
00:22:23.301 --> 00:22:24.885
Only one bus runs on this line.

359
00:22:24.886 --> 00:22:27.429
You didn't take the last one
'cause your marks were bad.

360
00:22:27.430 --> 00:22:30.099
One guy had a locked briefcase.
the other two didn't have anything.

361
00:22:31.851 --> 00:22:33.226
The woman at the
end of this bench

362
00:22:33.227 --> 00:22:37.272
has an unclasped purse and a four-year-old
taking up most of her attention.

363
00:22:37.273 --> 00:22:39.816
Easy pickings.

364
00:22:39.817 --> 00:22:41.443
Are you a cop?

365
00:22:41.444 --> 00:22:44.112
Don't need to be to see
your clumsy approach.

366
00:22:44.113 --> 00:22:46.198
Exact fare in quarters?

367
00:22:46.199 --> 00:22:50.535
What teenager after 1994 walks
around with quarters in their pocket?

368
00:22:50.536 --> 00:22:52.370
No.

369
00:22:52.371 --> 00:22:54.372
You're new at this.

370
00:22:54.373 --> 00:22:56.459
If you were a pro.
you'd have a bus pass.

371
00:22:58.628 --> 00:23:00.254
What are you gonna do?

372
00:23:06.469 --> 00:23:07.678
Here.

373
00:23:08.638 --> 00:23:10.431
You need money. right? Take it.

374
00:23:11.724 --> 00:23:12.891
Then go get a job.

375
00:23:12.892 --> 00:23:15.769
Because the next guy who catches you
stealing might not give you a hundred.

376
00:23:15.770 --> 00:23:17.688
He might give you a beating.

377
00:23:18.815 --> 00:23:20.024
Thanks.

378
00:23:21.943 --> 00:23:24.403
[suspenseful music playing]

379
00:23:25.738 --> 00:23:27.156
[horn honking]

380
00:23:40.086 --> 00:23:41.503
Give me your phone.

381
00:23:41.504 --> 00:23:43.673
[phone ringing]

382
00:23:44.924 --> 00:23:47.342
110th Special Investigators.
Warrant Officer Powell speaking.

383
00:23:47.343 --> 00:23:50.178
This is Jack Reacher. I need to
speak to your C.O. immediately.

384
00:23:50.179 --> 00:23:52.556
Sorry. sir. Major
Turner is unavailable.

385
00:23:52.557 --> 00:23:54.558
Tell her to call me back ASAP.

386
00:23:54.559 --> 00:23:56.059
<i>I'm calling in that
favor she owes me.</i>

387
00:23:56.060 --> 00:23:59.020
I can do that. sir. but she
won't get the note for a while.

388
00:23:59.021 --> 00:24:00.647
She's on assignment.

389
00:24:00.648 --> 00:24:03.942
Undercover and incommunicado
for at least two weeks.

390
00:24:03.943 --> 00:24:05.652
Is this really Major Reacher?

391
00:24:05.653 --> 00:24:08.196
Like. the Jack Reacher
who started the 110th?

392
00:24:08.197 --> 00:24:10.031
It is.

393
00:24:10.032 --> 00:24:11.783
I need your help. Powell.

394
00:24:11.784 --> 00:24:13.451
[Powell] <i>Whatever you need. sir.</i>

395
00:24:13.452 --> 00:24:16.830
- Run a license plate for me.
- <i>Of course. Shoot.</i>

396
00:24:16.831 --> 00:24:17.998
Civilian. Maine.

397
00:24:17.999 --> 00:24:19.750
Seven. Seven. Four.
Oh. Tango. Lima.

398
00:24:20.918 --> 00:24:22.336
Running now.

399
00:24:23.546 --> 00:24:25.255
Hey. uh... [chuckles softly]

400
00:24:25.256 --> 00:24:26.924
mind if I ask you a question?

401
00:24:28.467 --> 00:24:29.551
Shoot.

402
00:24:29.552 --> 00:24:33.513
Your old desk is still
here and there's a dent

403
00:24:33.514 --> 00:24:34.848
on the right-hand side.

404
00:24:34.849 --> 00:24:37.350
Legend is you made it
with a colonel's head.

405
00:24:37.351 --> 00:24:38.560
That true?

406
00:24:38.561 --> 00:24:41.730
David O'Donnell did that messing
around with Stan Lowrey's bowling ball.

407
00:24:41.731 --> 00:24:43.231
<i>Lowrey got back
at him by drawing</i>

408
00:24:43.232 --> 00:24:45.775
genitals on his face when
O'Donnell fell asleep on the couch.

409
00:24:45.776 --> 00:24:49.238
Man. we've heard stories
about those guys. too.

410
00:24:50.323 --> 00:24:51.698
Looks like something's
up with their system.

411
00:24:51.699 --> 00:24:54.534
I can give you a call when I get
it. Can I reach you at this number?

412
00:24:54.535 --> 00:24:58.121
No. Take down where I'm staying.

413
00:24:58.122 --> 00:25:00.917
[distant train horn blowing]

414
00:25:04.921 --> 00:25:06.755
[banging on door]

415
00:25:06.756 --> 00:25:09.008
[man] Federal agents. Open up.

416
00:25:39.622 --> 00:25:41.123
[grunts]

417
00:25:47.255 --> 00:25:49.257
[tense music playing]

418
00:25:53.177 --> 00:25:54.719
Where you going. Mr. Reacher?

419
00:25:54.720 --> 00:25:56.346
Who says my name's Reacher?

420
00:25:56.347 --> 00:25:57.973
Not the guy that
runs this shithole.

421
00:25:57.974 --> 00:26:00.392
He says you registered
as Rob Refsnyder.

422
00:26:00.393 --> 00:26:02.769
but you don't look much like
a middle infielder to me.

423
00:26:02.770 --> 00:26:05.146
Now. do you wanna
talk by the dumpster

424
00:26:05.147 --> 00:26:08.901
or can we find a place that
smells less like vomit?

425
00:26:15.074 --> 00:26:17.033
Nice place.

426
00:26:17.034 --> 00:26:19.077
- Motel 6 was booked.
- Mm.

427
00:26:19.078 --> 00:26:21.746
This is like a Motel 2.

428
00:26:21.747 --> 00:26:24.082
It's not like I invited
you here. Agent...?

429
00:26:24.083 --> 00:26:26.918
Duffy. Susan Duffy. The two
you left standing at the door

430
00:26:26.919 --> 00:26:29.963
with their dicks in their
hands are Eliot and Villanueva.

431
00:26:29.964 --> 00:26:31.715
Why'd you run?

432
00:26:31.716 --> 00:26:34.092
We identified ourselves
as federal agents.

433
00:26:34.093 --> 00:26:35.677
Anyone can say they're anything.

434
00:26:35.678 --> 00:26:39.556
This place attracts a
criminal element. I panicked.

435
00:26:39.557 --> 00:26:42.852
You don't seem like the
panicking type. Mr. Reacher.

436
00:26:44.061 --> 00:26:45.562
Just Reacher.

437
00:26:45.563 --> 00:26:48.064
Okay. Reacher. Why
do you use an alias?

438
00:26:48.065 --> 00:26:49.441
I like my privacy.

439
00:26:49.442 --> 00:26:52.027
- Is that why you gave no address?
- No.

440
00:26:52.028 --> 00:26:54.195
Then why no address?

441
00:26:54.196 --> 00:26:55.572
Because I don't have one.

442
00:26:55.573 --> 00:26:57.198
What are you doing in Maine?

443
00:26:57.199 --> 00:26:58.575
I wanted good lobster.

444
00:26:58.576 --> 00:27:01.619
- We're being serious.
- So am I.

445
00:27:01.620 --> 00:27:05.290
I was in Cape May. I had subpar lobster.
wanted better. so I came up here.

446
00:27:05.291 --> 00:27:08.835
- You think this is funny?
- I think this is a waste of my time.

447
00:27:08.836 --> 00:27:12.547
I don't know what you want from me.
but I know I want nothing from you.

448
00:27:12.548 --> 00:27:14.799
So I'm going back to my room.

449
00:27:14.800 --> 00:27:18.596
To wait for a call from
Warrant Officer Powell?

450
00:27:19.930 --> 00:27:21.639
Don't bother. It's not coming.

451
00:27:21.640 --> 00:27:24.768
So. why don't you drop your
seat warmer in that chair.

452
00:27:24.769 --> 00:27:27.938
You can finish feeding Daffy and
we can finish our conversation.

453
00:27:29.398 --> 00:27:31.191
Powell gave you up.

454
00:27:31.192 --> 00:27:35.320
He wouldn't roll till we threatened him
with obstructing a federal investigation.

455
00:27:35.321 --> 00:27:38.740
- Kid was nearly in tears.
- Fuckin' embarrassing.

456
00:27:38.741 --> 00:27:40.241
What federal investigation?

457
00:27:40.242 --> 00:27:43.912
We're looking into a rug import
business called Bizarre Bazaar.

458
00:27:43.913 --> 00:27:46.498
And the DEA think rugs aren't
the only thing they're importing.

459
00:27:46.499 --> 00:27:49.709
Several weeks ago. a high-level.
L.A.-based drug dealer

460
00:27:49.710 --> 00:27:52.587
flew to Maine for a meeting with
the owner of Bizarre Bazaar.

461
00:27:52.588 --> 00:27:55.840
Major drug runners don't travel
3.000 miles to buy carpets.

462
00:27:55.841 --> 00:27:58.259
So we figure the owner of
Bizarre Bazaar is his supplier.

463
00:27:58.260 --> 00:28:01.054
Which would make him responsible
for most of the poison

464
00:28:01.055 --> 00:28:03.807
being pumped into the
Western United States.

465
00:28:03.808 --> 00:28:05.683
Problem is. we can't dig
anything up on the guy.

466
00:28:05.684 --> 00:28:07.227
Not even an address.

467
00:28:07.228 --> 00:28:10.398
Figure the property's set up
under an LLC or something.

468
00:28:11.690 --> 00:28:12.982
What's this got to do with me?

469
00:28:12.983 --> 00:28:15.610
The license plate you ran
was screwed to the car

470
00:28:15.611 --> 00:28:17.987
that brought the Carpet
King to that meeting.

471
00:28:17.988 --> 00:28:20.824
We flagged the number on the
system so Powell tripped our alarm

472
00:28:20.825 --> 00:28:22.492
when he looked it up for you.

473
00:28:22.493 --> 00:28:23.785
Why were you checking the plate?

474
00:28:23.786 --> 00:28:25.745
Maybe the driver hit
my car and ran off.

475
00:28:25.746 --> 00:28:27.622
Did he hit your car and run off?

476
00:28:27.623 --> 00:28:29.041
I don't own a car.

477
00:28:33.170 --> 00:28:34.505
[grunts]

478
00:28:35.798 --> 00:28:37.090
Zachary Beck. You know him?

479
00:28:37.091 --> 00:28:40.427
[Duffy] Shit's sake. Eliot. you
don't give the guy we're questioning

480
00:28:40.428 --> 00:28:43.596
the name of the subject.
then ask if he knows him.

481
00:28:43.597 --> 00:28:45.557
Sorry. Shit.

482
00:28:45.558 --> 00:28:47.560
I don't know him.

483
00:28:49.687 --> 00:28:51.896
You recognize anyone here?

484
00:28:51.897 --> 00:28:53.065
No.

485
00:28:54.191 --> 00:28:56.651
[Duffy] I'll tell you what I think.
I think you saw someone in that car

486
00:28:56.652 --> 00:28:59.070
you did recognize and now
you're looking for them.

487
00:28:59.071 --> 00:29:00.239
So who was it?

488
00:29:01.907 --> 00:29:04.617
[Villanueva] According to Powell.
you were some kind of Army super-cop.

489
00:29:04.618 --> 00:29:06.995
We checked you out. More
awards than Tom Brady.

490
00:29:06.996 --> 00:29:08.121
Fuck that traitor.

491
00:29:08.122 --> 00:29:10.583
That's why we're coming to
you now. We need your help.

492
00:29:12.084 --> 00:29:14.711
Then you really
must be desperate.

493
00:29:14.712 --> 00:29:17.172
- Buddy. you don't know the half of it.
- [Reacher] And I don't want to.

494
00:29:17.173 --> 00:29:19.258
At least until you
do something for me.

495
00:29:20.968 --> 00:29:23.344
You're not the kind of guy
I wanna do a favor for.

496
00:29:23.345 --> 00:29:25.597
- Why is that?
- You're a pain in the ass.

497
00:29:25.598 --> 00:29:27.182
You answer questions
like an asshole.

498
00:29:27.183 --> 00:29:29.810
- You always so direct?
- You always so frustrating?

499
00:29:34.648 --> 00:29:36.733
So what can I do
for you. Reacher?

500
00:29:36.734 --> 00:29:38.985
Check hospital records
around Linton. Virginia

501
00:29:38.986 --> 00:29:41.279
on or just after
March 13th. 2012.

502
00:29:41.280 --> 00:29:43.865
- What are we looking for?
- An Asian American man in his 40s.

503
00:29:43.866 --> 00:29:45.283
brought in with
injuries consistent

504
00:29:45.284 --> 00:29:47.160
with a small-caliber
gunshot wound to the head.

505
00:29:47.161 --> 00:29:49.621
a high fall and drowning.
Look. you're the Feds.

506
00:29:49.622 --> 00:29:52.332
You've got resources. You
find something. call me.

507
00:29:52.333 --> 00:29:54.960
Maybe then we can talk
about what you need.

508
00:29:56.170 --> 00:29:58.047
[duck quacking]

509
00:30:01.425 --> 00:30:03.969
[crickets chirping]

510
00:30:07.389 --> 00:30:09.517
[room phone ringing]

511
00:30:12.019 --> 00:30:14.605
[ringing continues]

512
00:30:16.190 --> 00:30:18.107
So. we found your guy.

513
00:30:18.108 --> 00:30:22.820
Washed up on a beach barely alive
just south of. uh. whatsit. Virginia.

514
00:30:22.821 --> 00:30:25.073
- Linton.
- Whatever.

515
00:30:25.074 --> 00:30:26.908
Wounds matched your description.

516
00:30:26.909 --> 00:30:30.537
Small-caliber bullet lodged in his
skull. massive internal injuries.

517
00:30:30.538 --> 00:30:32.330
Some beachcomber found him.

518
00:30:32.331 --> 00:30:34.707
Doctors figure the
freezin' water saved him.

519
00:30:34.708 --> 00:30:36.793
- Hypothermia.
- Yup.

520
00:30:36.794 --> 00:30:38.211
Slowed his heart
so he didn't bleed.

521
00:30:38.212 --> 00:30:40.630
decreased oxygen demand
prevented brain damage.

522
00:30:40.631 --> 00:30:43.883
Took the docs about six months to
put Humpty Dumpty together again.

523
00:30:43.884 --> 00:30:46.261
He tell the medical staff
what happened to him?

524
00:30:46.262 --> 00:30:47.887
Claimed he didn't remember.

525
00:30:47.888 --> 00:30:48.930
File?

526
00:30:48.931 --> 00:30:52.058
Psychiatrists interviewed
the guy regularly

527
00:30:52.059 --> 00:30:53.268
when he was in the hospital.

528
00:30:53.269 --> 00:30:55.645
He stuck to his story.

529
00:30:55.646 --> 00:30:57.605
Do you see anyone else eating?

530
00:30:57.606 --> 00:30:59.774
What? I was at the Kinko's
first thing copying the files.

531
00:30:59.775 --> 00:31:02.277
- I didn't have time for break...
- They diagnosed traumatic amnesia.

532
00:31:02.278 --> 00:31:04.904
Thought he was probably genuinely
blank about the incident

533
00:31:04.905 --> 00:31:06.698
and the previous day or two.

534
00:31:06.699 --> 00:31:09.158
but they figured he must
remember things from before that.

535
00:31:09.159 --> 00:31:12.537
They got the impression maybe
he was pretending not to.

536
00:31:12.538 --> 00:31:14.914
They kept questioning
him. but he never cracked.

537
00:31:14.915 --> 00:31:16.958
Local cops look into it?

538
00:31:16.959 --> 00:31:19.669
County sheriff ran his prints.
but they weren't in the system.

539
00:31:19.670 --> 00:31:23.131
He also didn't match any missing
persons and no one came looking for him.

540
00:31:23.132 --> 00:31:24.632
so he stayed a John Doe.

541
00:31:24.633 --> 00:31:26.509
But from the way
you're eye-fucking him.

542
00:31:26.510 --> 00:31:28.137
I think you know his name.

543
00:31:31.640 --> 00:31:34.851
Fuck you. big boy. I showed
you mine. you show me yours.

544
00:31:34.852 --> 00:31:36.477
Or are there no rules
where you come from?

545
00:31:36.478 --> 00:31:38.104
I don't really
come from anywhere.

546
00:31:38.105 --> 00:31:40.064
Well. I did. And
on Emerson Street.

547
00:31:40.065 --> 00:31:42.818
if you didn't do what's right.
you got your ears boxed.

548
00:31:50.200 --> 00:31:52.410
Lieutenant Colonel
Francis Xavier Quinn.

549
00:31:52.411 --> 00:31:54.245
Military Intelligence.

550
00:31:54.246 --> 00:31:57.291
Picked up extra cash selling
military secrets to hostile nations.

551
00:31:58.626 --> 00:32:00.209
We were never able
to execute an arrest.

552
00:32:00.210 --> 00:32:03.379
- Who threw him off a cliff?
- Maybe an unsatisfied customer.

553
00:32:03.380 --> 00:32:05.049
He was in business
with bad people.

554
00:32:06.050 --> 00:32:08.730
If this guy was Army. his fingerprints
should've been in the system.

555
00:32:09.845 --> 00:32:11.304
He had deep connections
through M.I.

556
00:32:11.305 --> 00:32:14.057
Figure someone on the inside wiped 'em
from his file when he went on the run.

557
00:32:14.058 --> 00:32:15.851
Photos too. maybe.

558
00:32:16.852 --> 00:32:19.062
You saw Quinn in Beck's car.

559
00:32:19.063 --> 00:32:20.563
Yeah.

560
00:32:20.564 --> 00:32:22.524
[Duffy] And now
you wanna find him.

561
00:32:23.942 --> 00:32:25.526
Yeah.

562
00:32:25.527 --> 00:32:27.278
[Duffy] So maybe we can
help each other out.

563
00:32:27.279 --> 00:32:29.073
Let's take a walk.

564
00:32:34.328 --> 00:32:37.205
Look. I think I can trust you.

565
00:32:37.206 --> 00:32:39.625
but I'm trying to
figure out for sure.

566
00:32:40.793 --> 00:32:42.251
Why?

567
00:32:42.252 --> 00:32:44.379
Because I screwed up.

568
00:32:44.380 --> 00:32:48.299
Weeks of surveillance on Darien
Prado. he's the L.A. drug dealer.

569
00:32:48.300 --> 00:32:51.260
all inadmissible because
of a bad warrant.

570
00:32:51.261 --> 00:32:53.262
How'd that happen?

571
00:32:53.263 --> 00:32:56.557
We surveilled and filmed him from
what we thought was public land...

572
00:32:56.558 --> 00:32:59.143
national forest.
middle of nowhere...

573
00:32:59.144 --> 00:33:02.355
but it abutted private property.

574
00:33:02.356 --> 00:33:04.982
We were 20 feet over the
line and didn't know it.

575
00:33:04.983 --> 00:33:07.860
Warrant didn't let
us film from there.

576
00:33:07.861 --> 00:33:09.821
You misread the surveyor's map?

577
00:33:09.822 --> 00:33:12.365
It was a real shit show. okay?

578
00:33:12.366 --> 00:33:16.369
Ton of work down the crapper and
the DEA pulled us off the case.

579
00:33:16.370 --> 00:33:18.204
Now you're working
it off the books?

580
00:33:18.205 --> 00:33:21.290
[grunts] I don't
let bad guys walk.

581
00:33:21.291 --> 00:33:23.710
And I'm a team leader. No
one's watchin' my day-to-day.

582
00:33:23.711 --> 00:33:26.879
So now you're focused on Beck?

583
00:33:26.880 --> 00:33:30.216
[sighs] Prado flew all the
way out here to meet with him.

584
00:33:30.217 --> 00:33:32.385
so Beck could be a bigger fish.

585
00:33:32.386 --> 00:33:35.513
And if we net him. we
get Prado too. right?

586
00:33:35.514 --> 00:33:38.933
But Beck turned out to be a
ghost. Can't find out shit on him.

587
00:33:38.934 --> 00:33:42.311
So I got the bright idea
to reach out to an old C.I.

588
00:33:42.312 --> 00:33:45.231
Something tells me that didn't
work out like you planned.

589
00:33:45.232 --> 00:33:47.984
It's this kid named
Teresa Daniel.

590
00:33:47.985 --> 00:33:50.737
Few years ago. she was tricked
by her scumbag boyfriend

591
00:33:50.738 --> 00:33:53.072
into delivering car
parts stuffed with coke.

592
00:33:53.073 --> 00:33:54.574
She had no idea.

593
00:33:54.575 --> 00:33:58.536
I busted her. flipped her. turned
out to be the best C.I. I ever had.

594
00:33:58.537 --> 00:34:02.039
This kid is so innocent.
so unassuming...

595
00:34:02.040 --> 00:34:05.710
- No one suspects she's a plant.
- No one. She's a natural C.I.

596
00:34:05.711 --> 00:34:09.464
So when I saw Bizarre Bazaar had a
help wanted ad online for a secretary.

597
00:34:09.465 --> 00:34:10.965
I called Teresa.

598
00:34:10.966 --> 00:34:13.342
She lives with her grandmother.
she takes care of her.

599
00:34:13.343 --> 00:34:15.762
so I knew she needed money.

600
00:34:15.763 --> 00:34:18.014
She got the job at
Bizarre Bazaar's warehouse

601
00:34:18.015 --> 00:34:21.517
and was gonna just report back
what Beck was up to in there.

602
00:34:21.518 --> 00:34:23.020
But?

603
00:34:25.314 --> 00:34:28.025
About a week ago.
she disappeared.

604
00:34:29.318 --> 00:34:32.528
I don't hear from her. her
grandma's got no idea where she is.

605
00:34:32.529 --> 00:34:35.865
She called Bizarre Bazaar. but they
said she never showed up for work.

606
00:34:35.866 --> 00:34:39.286
so the old lady's sure her
granddaughter's using again.

607
00:34:40.370 --> 00:34:41.871
But you think
there's more to it.

608
00:34:41.872 --> 00:34:44.832
I know junkies. Teresa
was past all that.

609
00:34:44.833 --> 00:34:46.834
She'd turned it around.

610
00:34:46.835 --> 00:34:48.836
I think she got caught
snooping on Beck

611
00:34:48.837 --> 00:34:50.880
and something happened to her.

612
00:34:50.881 --> 00:34:53.883
I gotta find out what. but no
judge is gonna issue a warrant

613
00:34:53.884 --> 00:34:56.052
to search a prominent
local businessman

614
00:34:56.053 --> 00:34:58.513
over an ex-druggie
blowing off work.

615
00:34:58.514 --> 00:35:01.225
Like. she's 20. but
she's still just a kid.

616
00:35:03.393 --> 00:35:06.771
Look. She wears these.
uh. giant hoop earrings

617
00:35:06.772 --> 00:35:08.649
like my niece and her friends.

618
00:35:10.692 --> 00:35:12.569
Why are you showing me this?

619
00:35:14.154 --> 00:35:15.905
'Cause you need to know
what she looks like

620
00:35:15.906 --> 00:35:19.325
when I put you inside Beck's
operation to find her.

621
00:35:19.326 --> 00:35:21.994
I hate to break it to you. but
if Teresa was taken by someone

622
00:35:21.995 --> 00:35:25.164
associated with Xavier Quinn.
odds are you're too late.

623
00:35:25.165 --> 00:35:27.166
Why would you say
something like that to me?

624
00:35:27.167 --> 00:35:28.918
Because you're too
smart to lie to.

625
00:35:28.919 --> 00:35:31.045
You'd see through it.

626
00:35:31.046 --> 00:35:32.213
He's that bad?

627
00:35:32.214 --> 00:35:34.423
He's the single worst
person I've ever known.

628
00:35:34.424 --> 00:35:37.051
Well. all the more reason
for you to get on board.

629
00:35:37.052 --> 00:35:38.469
You need to find Quinn.

630
00:35:38.470 --> 00:35:41.764
While you're doing that.
you can help me find Teresa.

631
00:35:41.765 --> 00:35:45.644
You know. I'm not just a
pretty face. I have a plan.

632
00:35:48.021 --> 00:35:50.398
[Duffy] Zachary
Beck's son. Richard.

633
00:35:50.399 --> 00:35:52.608
Five years ago.
he was kidnapped.

634
00:35:52.609 --> 00:35:55.528
You know how often people get
kidnapped in America these days?

635
00:35:55.529 --> 00:35:58.489
Could be a turf war
thing. Rival drug dealers.

636
00:35:58.490 --> 00:36:01.200
Especially since the kidnappers
cut off the kid's ear

637
00:36:01.201 --> 00:36:04.370
and mailed it to Beck. who. by
the way. never went to the cops.

638
00:36:04.371 --> 00:36:06.581
How do you know about it. then?

639
00:36:06.582 --> 00:36:10.793
Well. you walk around a college campus
with a missing ear and kids ask questions.

640
00:36:10.794 --> 00:36:14.255
Richard answered some of 'em.
and one of his classmates talked

641
00:36:14.256 --> 00:36:16.591
in exchange for us dropping
some minor drug charges.

642
00:36:16.592 --> 00:36:20.344
So the Beck kid's had it rough.
What's he got to do with your plan?

643
00:36:20.345 --> 00:36:22.471
You're gonna get in with Beck

644
00:36:22.472 --> 00:36:24.974
by saving his son from
getting kidnapped again.

645
00:36:24.975 --> 00:36:28.352
- Undercover informant?
- Yeah. what's the problem?

646
00:36:28.353 --> 00:36:30.104
The last one you
had went missing.

647
00:36:30.105 --> 00:36:33.983
You remember what I said earlier
about you being an asshole?

648
00:36:33.984 --> 00:36:35.943
You're doing it right now.

649
00:36:35.944 --> 00:36:40.114
[♪ Eli "Paperboy"
Reed: "Cut Ya Down"]

650
00:36:40.115 --> 00:36:43.034
[Villanueva] All right. so we get
a solid car from the DEA impound.

651
00:36:43.035 --> 00:36:46.495
ram the hell outta the bodyguard's
car. pin it so that it can't move.

652
00:36:46.496 --> 00:36:48.080
We still gotta
deal with the guy.

653
00:36:48.081 --> 00:36:49.874
[Duffy] And he's
no pushover either.

654
00:36:49.875 --> 00:36:52.793
Got a jacket and a half:
aggravated assault. armed robbery.

655
00:36:52.794 --> 00:36:54.128
He'll know how to use his gun.

656
00:36:54.129 --> 00:36:56.047
Great. How we gonna
keep from getting shot?

657
00:36:56.048 --> 00:36:58.049
'Cause we can't
just kill the man.

658
00:36:58.050 --> 00:37:00.385
Hey. here he is. Gimme.

659
00:37:01.803 --> 00:37:04.221
- What's this shit? I said Dink's.
- A doughnut's a doughnut.

660
00:37:04.222 --> 00:37:05.389
Shut your filthy mouth.

661
00:37:05.390 --> 00:37:07.099
Okay. fine. I'll
eat 'em all. then.

662
00:37:07.100 --> 00:37:08.351
Didn't say I didn't want 'em.

663
00:37:08.352 --> 00:37:10.811
- You take your Lipitor today?
- Still waiting on the refill.

664
00:37:10.812 --> 00:37:13.230
Oh.

665
00:37:13.231 --> 00:37:16.025
Let's say the impact rings
the bodyguard's bell.

666
00:37:16.026 --> 00:37:18.653
Doesn't mean he won't
get a few shots off.

667
00:37:18.654 --> 00:37:21.907
Duffy's right. We need more.

668
00:37:23.867 --> 00:37:25.618
In Kuwait. we'd used
flashbang grenades

669
00:37:25.619 --> 00:37:28.496
when we wanted to keep a
target alive for interrogation.

670
00:37:28.497 --> 00:37:31.749
Bodyguard won't be seriously injured. but
he'll be in no condition to retaliate.

671
00:37:31.750 --> 00:37:35.711
It'll blow out the windows.
really sell the lie to Richard.

672
00:37:35.712 --> 00:37:38.714
And it'll create a job opening.
Beck will need a new bodyguard.

673
00:37:38.715 --> 00:37:40.508
Okay. sorry. I'm confused.

674
00:37:40.509 --> 00:37:42.218
- Shocking.
- [Eliot] If the bodyguard isn't really dead.

675
00:37:42.219 --> 00:37:44.553
he can just go tell Beck
what actually happened.

676
00:37:44.554 --> 00:37:46.973
So how do we get around that?

677
00:37:46.974 --> 00:37:49.016
We hold him indefinitely.

678
00:37:49.017 --> 00:37:51.686
Without so much as the
right to a phone call.

679
00:37:51.687 --> 00:37:54.605
Pretty sure the Constitution
says you can't do that.

680
00:37:54.606 --> 00:37:56.023
[Reacher] You're DEA.

681
00:37:56.024 --> 00:37:58.484
Grab some drugs from
Evidence. plant it in his car.

682
00:37:58.485 --> 00:38:00.778
say he was buying it from
some Central American dealer.

683
00:38:00.779 --> 00:38:02.405
then it becomes a
narco-terrorism case.

684
00:38:02.406 --> 00:38:03.864
You can hold him
as long as you want

685
00:38:03.865 --> 00:38:05.865
without formal charges and
no right to an attorney.

686
00:38:07.202 --> 00:38:09.328
- The law allows for that?
- It's kind of a gray area.

687
00:38:09.329 --> 00:38:12.541
A mouse's asshole is a gray
area. This is barely legal.

688
00:38:14.584 --> 00:38:16.585
But I don't think
we have a choice.

689
00:38:16.586 --> 00:38:19.131
And while we got him. we
can question him. Good idea.

690
00:38:20.632 --> 00:38:22.259
Not just a pretty face.

691
00:38:23.802 --> 00:38:27.013
Okay. that takes care
of our bodyguard.

692
00:38:27.014 --> 00:38:28.515
Who's playing our kidnapper?

693
00:38:31.852 --> 00:38:32.977
I'll do it.

694
00:38:32.978 --> 00:38:35.855
[scoffs] No. This one's out of
your comfort zone. precious.

695
00:38:35.856 --> 00:38:38.566
There's gonna be smashing
cars. flying glass.

696
00:38:38.567 --> 00:38:40.067
Villy. can you reel in
someone pulling a pension?

697
00:38:40.068 --> 00:38:41.068
No. No. Hell no.

698
00:38:41.069 --> 00:38:42.069
Excuse me?

699
00:38:43.363 --> 00:38:44.530
I'm the one who
messed up the warrant.

700
00:38:44.531 --> 00:38:49.118
I'm the one who read the surveyor's
map wrong. set us up on private land.

701
00:38:49.119 --> 00:38:50.912
I'm gonna fix this.

702
00:38:53.040 --> 00:38:56.500
No brains. some balls.
Fine. you're our kidnapper.

703
00:38:56.501 --> 00:38:59.754
[Reacher] Okay. You'll make a move
for Richard. How do I stop you?

704
00:38:59.755 --> 00:39:02.424
He'll have a front row seat.
and fake fights look fake.

705
00:39:03.550 --> 00:39:04.843
[Villanueva] We shoot him.

706
00:39:06.178 --> 00:39:07.803
[Duffy] Seriously?

707
00:39:07.804 --> 00:39:09.972
You're a fucking raccoon.

708
00:39:09.973 --> 00:39:12.266
<i>♪ Cut 'em down. tell
'em God Almighty's ♪</i>

709
00:39:12.267 --> 00:39:14.310
<i>♪ Gonna cut 'em down ♪</i>

710
00:39:14.311 --> 00:39:16.228
Are you sure this is safe?

711
00:39:16.229 --> 00:39:19.607
My buddy's kid uses 'em all the
time in these indie films he makes.

712
00:39:19.608 --> 00:39:22.860
- Buddy's kid.
- It's top quality stuff.

713
00:39:22.861 --> 00:39:24.738
Okay. don't move.

714
00:39:26.281 --> 00:39:29.326
Okay. point your finger
at the kid. say "bang."

715
00:39:30.452 --> 00:39:32.119
No.

716
00:39:32.120 --> 00:39:33.537
Christ's sakes. Bang.

717
00:39:33.538 --> 00:39:35.414
[Villanueva] Is
that great or what?

718
00:39:35.415 --> 00:39:37.667
I can hide nearby and
set off the charges.

719
00:39:38.919 --> 00:39:41.420
Shit. Villy! Warn-warn me first!

720
00:39:41.421 --> 00:39:43.924
You're gonna give him a
heart attack. Hand it over.

721
00:39:45.133 --> 00:39:48.719
Jesus! Sh... Come on.
guys. it's not funny.

722
00:39:48.720 --> 00:39:50.513
Funny to me. Boys?

723
00:39:50.514 --> 00:39:51.847
Me. too.

724
00:39:51.848 --> 00:39:53.642
Kind of funny.

725
00:39:54.976 --> 00:39:56.102
<i>♪ Ugh...</i>

726
00:39:56.103 --> 00:39:59.480
[Reacher] After the fake
grenade blast and a gun fight.

727
00:39:59.481 --> 00:40:01.607
Richard won't come
with me easily.

728
00:40:01.608 --> 00:40:03.651
- [Villanueva] You're making an assumption...
- [Reacher] No.

729
00:40:03.652 --> 00:40:05.945
In an investigation.
assumptions kill.

730
00:40:05.946 --> 00:40:08.239
I'm making a reasonable
prediction that the college kid.

731
00:40:08.240 --> 00:40:10.991
who was just almost abducted
for the second time in his life.

732
00:40:10.992 --> 00:40:12.952
will be scared to death and
want the guy who saved him

733
00:40:12.953 --> 00:40:14.578
to take him to the cops.

734
00:40:14.579 --> 00:40:17.373
If he insists on that. this
is all a waste of time.

735
00:40:17.374 --> 00:40:19.084
He's not wrong. Villy.

736
00:40:20.877 --> 00:40:23.587
Refuse to do it. You'll be
driving. just take him home.

737
00:40:23.588 --> 00:40:26.590
[Reacher] That's suspicious. I'm trying
to infiltrate his dad's operation.

738
00:40:26.591 --> 00:40:29.093
We need as little
suspicion as possible.

739
00:40:29.094 --> 00:40:30.262
<i>♪ Ugh...</i>

740
00:40:31.346 --> 00:40:32.847
So what do we do?

741
00:40:32.848 --> 00:40:35.488
We take the option of going to the
police completely off the table.

742
00:40:36.810 --> 00:40:37.811
How?

743
00:40:39.437 --> 00:40:41.313
I kill a cop.

744
00:40:41.314 --> 00:40:43.441
[dramatic music playing]

745
00:40:44.860 --> 00:40:49.113
Time of day we're doing this.
streets should be mostly empty.

746
00:40:49.114 --> 00:40:51.448
We should give Eliot an Uzi.

747
00:40:51.449 --> 00:40:55.286
Rat-tat-tat of a machine gun
will scatter anyone nearby.

748
00:40:55.287 --> 00:40:57.079
Find me a panel van.

749
00:40:57.080 --> 00:41:00.207
I'll dive behind it for cover.
Eliot can really light it up.

750
00:41:00.208 --> 00:41:02.043
put on a convincing show.

751
00:41:04.171 --> 00:41:06.173
You know blanks alone
won't sell this.

752
00:41:07.465 --> 00:41:09.842
Was wondering who was
gonna say it first.

753
00:41:09.843 --> 00:41:11.886
I'll mix in some live ammo.

754
00:41:11.887 --> 00:41:14.680
I'll ditch the spent casings
before I get to Beck's house

755
00:41:14.681 --> 00:41:16.515
so they don't
notice a difference.

756
00:41:16.516 --> 00:41:18.434
That lets me put a couple
slugs into the radiator

757
00:41:18.435 --> 00:41:20.269
of the kidnapper's ride. and
I can shoot out the tires

758
00:41:20.270 --> 00:41:22.104
before I kill Eliot and
Villanueva with blanks.

759
00:41:22.105 --> 00:41:23.565
Hmm.

760
00:41:27.819 --> 00:41:29.279
I like this plan.

761
00:41:30.363 --> 00:41:33.991
I don't like this plan.
Using live ammo is insane.

762
00:41:33.992 --> 00:41:36.243
What if you forget how
many shots you fired?

763
00:41:36.244 --> 00:41:37.786
There could be a real
one left in the chamber

764
00:41:37.787 --> 00:41:39.496
when you turn the
gun on me or Eliot.

765
00:41:39.497 --> 00:41:40.789
You think about that. hotshot?

766
00:41:40.790 --> 00:41:42.499
Yeah. I did.

767
00:41:42.500 --> 00:41:45.419
- Did you get me the gun I asked for?
- Here.

768
00:41:45.420 --> 00:41:47.088
So what?

769
00:41:50.425 --> 00:41:52.135
You got a pocket knife?

770
00:42:03.480 --> 00:42:06.398
Now I always know exactly
where the blanks start.

771
00:42:06.399 --> 00:42:08.150
[dramatic music playing]

772
00:42:08.151 --> 00:42:10.237
♪ ♪

773
00:42:11.696 --> 00:42:13.656
Best impound had to offer.

774
00:42:13.657 --> 00:42:15.574
[Villanueva] Minivan will
be right by the dumpster.

775
00:42:15.575 --> 00:42:18.495
Coat hanger will be
on top of the garbage.

776
00:42:19.579 --> 00:42:21.665
Door will be unlocked.
Just pretend to jimmy it.

777
00:42:23.208 --> 00:42:24.959
What's wrong?

778
00:42:24.960 --> 00:42:27.044
I don't know how
to hot-wire a car.

779
00:42:27.045 --> 00:42:29.838
We'll loosen the shroud on the
steering column. pre-strip the wires.

780
00:42:29.839 --> 00:42:31.966
You touch them together.
you're an instant bad guy.

781
00:42:31.967 --> 00:42:34.843
I've also been thinking
about the street layout.

782
00:42:34.844 --> 00:42:37.179
Your best vantage point.
before everything jumps off.

783
00:42:37.180 --> 00:42:39.473
is from inside the record shop.

784
00:42:39.474 --> 00:42:41.141
But you'll need a reason
to hang out in there.

785
00:42:41.142 --> 00:42:42.393
And?

786
00:42:42.394 --> 00:42:44.104
And I got you covered.

787
00:42:52.028 --> 00:42:53.696
What am I supposed
to do with these?

788
00:42:53.697 --> 00:42:55.197
Record store buys old vinyl.

789
00:42:55.198 --> 00:42:57.284
Just pretend you want
to sell my collection.

790
00:43:00.287 --> 00:43:01.328
Won't work.

791
00:43:01.329 --> 00:43:02.705
Why not?

792
00:43:02.706 --> 00:43:05.667
'Cause no one'll believe anyone thinks
they can get a nickel for this crap.

793
00:43:06.501 --> 00:43:07.502
Fuck you.

794
00:43:13.091 --> 00:43:15.552
<i>Ethel Merman Disco Album?</i>

795
00:43:23.727 --> 00:43:25.811
No duck tonight?

796
00:43:25.812 --> 00:43:28.273
Probably doesn't want to
be a part of this plan.

797
00:43:29.816 --> 00:43:31.401
[grunts]

798
00:43:33.236 --> 00:43:34.945
Don't think we can pull it off?

799
00:43:34.946 --> 00:43:38.032
If we can set off the bullet
hits at exactly the right time.

800
00:43:38.033 --> 00:43:40.784
and if no one
actually gets shot.

801
00:43:40.785 --> 00:43:44.204
and if you can keep that
bodyguard pinned down long enough.

802
00:43:44.205 --> 00:43:45.831
I only see two
potential problems.

803
00:43:45.832 --> 00:43:48.709
- Okay. hit me.
- Cops.

804
00:43:48.710 --> 00:43:51.879
Shootout will be over pretty fast. but
they'll definitely show up after the fact.

805
00:43:51.880 --> 00:43:54.673
And I'll be there to tell them
it's a drug deal gone south.

806
00:43:54.674 --> 00:43:57.593
it's an active DEA investigation.
and our jurisdiction.

807
00:43:57.594 --> 00:43:58.844
What about campus security?

808
00:43:58.845 --> 00:44:00.846
Rent-a-cops like to
play hero sometimes.

809
00:44:00.847 --> 00:44:03.515
Small department with
no regular patrol.

810
00:44:03.516 --> 00:44:05.476
I mean. if they happen
to cross your path.

811
00:44:05.477 --> 00:44:07.354
you'll have to dispose of them.

812
00:44:09.814 --> 00:44:11.358
Without causing injury.

813
00:44:15.403 --> 00:44:16.737
What's the second problem?

814
00:44:16.738 --> 00:44:19.031
Communication.

815
00:44:19.032 --> 00:44:20.367
How do we stay in touch?

816
00:44:22.869 --> 00:44:26.663
I think I got the size right.

817
00:44:26.664 --> 00:44:29.666
You know what they say about a
man with big feet. don't you?

818
00:44:29.667 --> 00:44:33.963
More room in his boot heel
to hide a secret phone.

819
00:44:35.590 --> 00:44:37.883
Government issue.
satellite-linked.

820
00:44:37.884 --> 00:44:39.885
pretty much untraceable.

821
00:44:39.886 --> 00:44:41.720
14-day battery life.

822
00:44:41.721 --> 00:44:45.516
If you need me. I am
just a phone call away.

823
00:44:45.517 --> 00:44:47.227
♪ ♪

824
00:44:52.732 --> 00:44:55.025
{\an8}[Duffy over phone] <i>You're
in? So he hired you?</i>

825
00:44:55.026 --> 00:44:57.986
{\an8}Yeah. Interesting job interview.

826
00:44:57.987 --> 00:45:00.030
Made me play Russian roulette.

827
00:45:00.031 --> 00:45:02.324
Probably thought it was
more theatrical that way.

828
00:45:02.325 --> 00:45:04.451
<i>Fuck. You did it?</i>

829
00:45:04.452 --> 00:45:05.994
I used my own gun.

830
00:45:05.995 --> 00:45:07.913
I had a chamber
marked. remember?

831
00:45:07.914 --> 00:45:10.082
I put the bullet in that one so.
even with the cylinder closed.

832
00:45:10.083 --> 00:45:11.458
I always knew where it was.

833
00:45:11.459 --> 00:45:13.293
What if the one with
the bullet had come up?

834
00:45:13.294 --> 00:45:16.297
<i>I'd have shot the armed guy behind
me and tried to fight my way out.</i>

835
00:45:17.882 --> 00:45:19.716
- Any leads on Quinn?
<i>- Not yet.</i>

836
00:45:19.717 --> 00:45:21.343
How's the bodyguard?

837
00:45:21.344 --> 00:45:23.596
[Duffy] He's in
the adjoining room.

838
00:45:25.181 --> 00:45:27.683
We patched him up.
took a few runs at him.

839
00:45:27.684 --> 00:45:29.268
but he's not saying shit.

840
00:45:29.269 --> 00:45:31.395
<i>Claims he spends most
of his time with Richard</i>

841
00:45:31.396 --> 00:45:34.022
<i>- and has no idea what we're talking about.</i>
- You believe him?

842
00:45:34.023 --> 00:45:35.983
I don't know.

843
00:45:35.984 --> 00:45:38.110
Well. I might have
a lead on the girl.

844
00:45:38.111 --> 00:45:40.988
Beck's head of security carried
a plate of food outside.

845
00:45:40.989 --> 00:45:42.489
Could've been taking it
to the carriage house

846
00:45:42.490 --> 00:45:44.658
where I think there's
a hidden cellar.

847
00:45:44.659 --> 00:45:46.785
I'll wait till
everyone's asleep.

848
00:45:46.786 --> 00:45:48.370
At 3:00 a.m.. I'll check it out.

849
00:45:48.371 --> 00:45:50.331
Keep me posted.

850
00:45:51.458 --> 00:45:52.625
[phone beeps]

851
00:45:54.335 --> 00:45:56.337
[clock ticking]

852
00:46:00.633 --> 00:46:02.635
[suspenseful music playing]

853
00:46:13.605 --> 00:46:15.607
♪ ♪

854
00:46:22.739 --> 00:46:23.948
[grunts]

855
00:46:37.462 --> 00:46:39.506
♪ ♪

856
00:46:51.893 --> 00:46:53.895
[panting]

857
00:46:57.690 --> 00:46:59.692
♪ ♪

858
00:47:20.046 --> 00:47:22.674
[grunting softly]

859
00:47:28.680 --> 00:47:29.722
[grunts]

860
00:47:59.127 --> 00:48:01.170
♪ ♪

